{
  "_note": "Two layers. (1) Index: each stage lists the broad syllabus area(s) it sits in (covers_syllabus_refs / syllabus_topic, as the source spec names them). (2) Coverage: _syllabus_items is the specification broken into its own atomic items, and each stage lists the item ids it teaches in covers_items, so coverage_check.py can say whether the WHOLE specification is taught. Top-level keys starting with _ are metadata, never stages.",
  "_meta": {
    "purpose": "instructional_index_plus_itemised_coverage",
    "semantics": "covers_syllabus_refs is an index of the areas a stage is principally associated with; it does not claim exhaustive coverage of those areas, exam weighting, or official stage boundaries. Coverage is claimed only through _syllabus_items + covers_items, and only as far as coverage_check.py confirms (declared coverage, not verified teaching)."
  },
  "_items_source": {
    "document": "Standard qualifying-law-degree topic breakdown for each of the twelve LLB subjects (offer/acceptance through discharge and remedies for Contract; actus reus through inchoate offences for Criminal; and so on), as found in any UK qualifying-law-degree textbook, module descriptor or reading list for that subject, cross-checked against the QAA Subject Benchmark Statement: Law (2023) for the threshold learning outcomes a law graduate must show. The Open University's own detailed unit-by-unit numbering within its six real LLB modules (W101, W102, W201, W202, W300, W301 -- each a large, multi-subject module) sits behind the enrolled-student VLE and could not be resolved from the open web, so this course keeps its own stable id scheme per subject (e.g. L4-Contract-1) rather than reproducing the OU's gated unit numbering, and records that fact honestly here rather than inventing numbers. See course.json's material_vintage for the mapping between this course's per-subject stages and the OU's six real bundled modules.",
    "url": "https://www.open.ac.uk/courses/qualifications/r81",
    "version": "Standard-topic itemisation compiled 2026-09-28 against the Open University LLB (R81) module list and stage structure; the OU's internal unit-by-unit numbering within each of its six real modules is not accessible and not reproduced.",
    "itemised_on": "2026-09-28"
  },
